<p class="copy">
	Drone craft are the basic robotic infrastructure of ships and stations, handling everything from goods transportation and routine maintenance to security and inspection. Ranging from the size of a small ball to several meters across, they are built for specific tasks rather than any standardized design. A drone might be little more than a camera and a manipulator arm, while others are capable of hauling cargo, repairing hulls, or patrolling a station's exterior.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	They are ubiquitous across the surfaces of ships and stations, crawling over hulls, floating lazily around larger structures, or darting along wires and guideways laid for their use. Most are simple enough to operate autonomously, though larger or more specialized craft can be remotely piloted when the task calls for a human touch.
</p>
